From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tonrakun <tonrakun@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:37:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Kodama: chunk packet cache

License: GPL-3.0

PlayerChunkSender#sendChunk reuses one ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket
per chunk for every player it is sent to instead of building it again.
The packet still goes through the normal netty encoder and compressor.

An entry is valid for the modification counter of the LevelChunk it was
built at. The counter is raised when a block, block entity or anything
else that marks the chunk unsaved changes and on every light update that
Starlight reports; the entry is also dropped when the chunk unloads, when
it is older than max-age-seconds, and by least recently used eviction once
the estimated size exceeds max-mb. Packets that anti-xray modifies for a
player are built as before and never cached.

The cache is off while ProtocolLib or PacketEvents is enabled, because a
listener could change a packet that is shared by several players, unless
ignore-packet-plugins is set. A failure disables only the cache through
FeatureGuard and the packet is built normally.

Controlled by chunk-loading.packet-cache.*; /kodama status shows whether
the cache is active (and why not), hits, misses, invalidations, entries
and size.

